from (values
('127.397.d.7.A',4,'The purpose of a bearing in a rotating shaft is to:','["store energy", "add friction", "stop the shaft", "reduce friction and support the load"]'::jsonb,3,'Bearings let shafts turn smoothly.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.B',3,'When two meshed gears turn, they rotate in:','["opposite directions", "the same direction", "no direction", "random directions"]'::jsonb,0,'Adjacent meshed gears reverse direction.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.B',4,'A pulley with a belt is a good choice for moving power between shafts that are:','["touching", "some distance apart", "the same shaft", "welded together"]'::jsonb,1,'Belts bridge a distance between shafts.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.C',3,'Which of these is a simple machine?','["battery", "thermostat", "inclined plane", "transistor"]'::jsonb,2,'The six simple machines include the inclined plane.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.C',4,'A screw is best described as an inclined plane that is:','["made of springs", "flat", "cut in half", "wrapped around a cylinder"]'::jsonb,3,'A screw''s thread is a wrapped ramp.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.D',3,'A spring scale is used to measure:','["force", "distance", "temperature", "time"]'::jsonb,0,'Spring scales measure force.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.D',4,'To measure how far a load is lifted by a lever, an engineer uses a:','["stopwatch", "ruler or tape measure", "scale of force", "voltmeter"]'::jsonb,1,'Distance is measured with a ruler.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.E',3,'A machine lifts a 50-newton load 3 meters. The work done is:','["53 joules", "16.7 joules", "150 joules", "47 joules"]'::jsonb,2,'Work = force x distance = 50 x 3.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.E',4,'A motor does 600 joules of work in 20 seconds. Its power is:','["0.03 watts", "580 watts", "12,000 watts", "30 watts"]'::jsonb,3,'Power = work / time = 600 / 20.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.F',3,'A machine takes in 200 joules and delivers 150 joules of useful work. Its efficiency is:','["75 percent", "133 percent", "25 percent", "50 percent"]'::jsonb,0,'150 / 200 = 0.75.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.F',4,'The missing energy in a less-than-100-percent efficient machine is mostly lost as:','["perfect motion", "heat from friction", "free energy", "extra work"]'::jsonb,1,'Friction converts energy to heat.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.G',3,'A gear with 10 teeth drives a gear with 40 teeth. The drive ratio is:','["1 to 4", "40 to 10 speed-up", "4 to 1", "10 to 40 speed-up"]'::jsonb,2,'40 / 10 = 4, a speed reduction.','original'),
('127.397.d.7.G',4,'A lever has an effort arm of 90 centimeters and a load arm of 30 centimeters. Its ideal mechanical advantage is:','["0.33", "60", "120", "3"]'::jsonb,3,'90 / 30 = 3.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.A',3,'Solar power is classified as a(n):','["renewable energy source", "nuclear fuel", "nonrenewable source", "fossil fuel"]'::jsonb,0,'Sunlight is replenished continually.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.A',4,'Which source is nonrenewable?','["hydropower", "coal", "geothermal", "wind"]'::jsonb,1,'Coal takes millions of years to form.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.B',3,'A device uses 100 watts for 5 seconds. The energy used is:','["95 joules", "105 joules", "500 joules", "20 joules"]'::jsonb,2,'Energy = power x time.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.B',4,'A 60-watt bulb runs for 10 hours. The energy used in watt-hours is:','["50", "6", "70", "600"]'::jsonb,3,'60 W x 10 h = 600 Wh.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.C',3,'Electrical energy in a heater is mainly converted to:','["thermal energy", "chemical energy", "light only", "sound only"]'::jsonb,0,'A heater turns electricity into heat.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.C',4,'In an electric motor, electrical energy is converted primarily into:','["food energy", "mechanical energy", "nuclear energy", "sound only"]'::jsonb,1,'Motors turn current into motion.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.D',3,'A circuit has 12 volts across a 4-ohm resistor. The current is:','["8 amperes", "48 amperes", "3 amperes", "0.33 amperes"]'::jsonb,2,'I = V / R = 12 / 4.','original'),
('127.397.d.8.D',4,'A 2-ampere current flows through a 6-ohm resistor. The voltage across it is:','["3 volts", "0.33 volts", "8 volts", "12 volts"]'::jsonb,3,'V = I x R = 2 x 6.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.A',3,'Energy management in a plant aims to:','["use energy efficiently and reduce waste", "stop all machines", "increase waste", "ignore costs"]'::jsonb,0,'Managing energy saves cost.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.A',4,'A building energy audit helps identify:','["staff birthdays", "where energy is being wasted", "paint choices", "parking spots"]'::jsonb,1,'Audits locate losses.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.B',3,'To pick an energy source for a remote sensor, an engineer first estimates the sensor''s:','["color", "weight of the manual", "power needs", "logo"]'::jsonb,2,'Match the source to the load.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.B',4,'A load needs 20 watts for 10 hours daily. The daily energy required is:','["2 watt-hours", "30 watt-hours", "0.5 watt-hours", "200 watt-hours"]'::jsonb,3,'20 x 10 = 200.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.C',3,'A solar panel paired with a battery lets a system keep running:','["at night", "with no storage", "without wiring", "only in sunlight"]'::jsonb,0,'The battery stores energy for when the sun is down.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.C',4,'Combining wind and solar in one design helps because their output peaks:','["only in winter", "at different times", "at the same time always", "never"]'::jsonb,1,'Complementary sources smooth supply.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.D',3,'A hydrogen fuel cell produces electricity, heat, and:','["ash", "coal", "water", "smoke"]'::jsonb,2,'Hydrogen plus oxygen yields water.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.D',4,'A fuel cell differs from a battery because it:','["has no electrodes", "never makes heat", "stores no chemicals ever", "is fed fuel continuously to keep producing power"]'::jsonb,3,'Fuel cells run as long as fuel is supplied.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.E',3,'Warm air rising from a heater and cool air sinking is an example of heat transfer by:','["convection", "magnetism", "conduction only", "radiation only"]'::jsonb,0,'Convection moves heat in fluids.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.E',4,'Heat from the sun reaching Earth through space is transferred by:','["conduction", "radiation", "convection", "pressure"]'::jsonb,1,'Radiation needs no medium.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.F',3,'A metal spoon in hot soup gets hot due to:','["radiation only", "convection only", "conduction", "sound"]'::jsonb,2,'Heat flows through solids by conduction.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.F',4,'A material with low thermal conductivity makes a good:','["heat sink", "conductor of heat", "wire", "insulator"]'::jsonb,3,'Low conductivity slows heat flow.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.G',3,'A transmission line has 2 ohms of resistance and carries 10 amperes. The power lost as heat is:','["200 watts", "20 watts", "12 watts", "5 watts"]'::jsonb,0,'P = I squared x R = 100 x 2.','original'),
('127.397.d.9.G',4,'Sending power at higher voltage reduces line losses because the current is:','["unchanged", "lower for the same power", "zero", "higher"]'::jsonb,1,'P = V x I, so higher V means lower I.','original'),
('127.397.d.10.A',3,'A book rests on a table. The table pushes up with a force called the:','["buoyant force", "friction force", "normal force", "tension"]'::jsonb,2,'The surface pushes perpendicular to itself.','original'),
